## The Wolf Among Us 2 at a glance

The Wolf Among Us 2 is Telltale's sequel to its 2013 narrative adventure The Wolf Among Us, which was based on the *Fables* comic books. You play Bigby Wolf, the sheriff of Fabletown, again. When we checked on 26 November 2026, the official Steam listing said **Coming soon** and gave no calendar date.

## What we know so far

- **Developer and publisher:** Telltale, according to Steam.
- **Release date:** not announced. Steam says "Coming soon" without a day, month or year.
- **Platforms:** the Steam listing is for Windows. Telltale's own game page says the game is also coming to other platforms, but we couldn't confirm which ones from the page.
- **Trailer:** the official announcement trailer is on the Steam page.
- **Language:** English, with full audio. It is the only language Steam lists.
- **Controls:** Steam lists full controller support.

## The story Telltale has described

The official description calls the game a "neon-noir" thriller. A deadly conspiracy breaks the uneasy peace among the Fables, the fairy-tale characters living in exile in Fabletown. Bigby is betrayed, framed and exiled, and has to work from the shadows to save the city.

The listing names some of the forces involved. A group called the Oz Gang is gaining power, and older forces are manipulating events in secret. The central question Telltale poses is whether the "monster within" Bigby will destroy what he is trying to protect, or turn out to be the key to saving it.

## Gameplay Telltale has confirmed

The store page lists these features:

- a dark neon-noir story
- more exploration and investigation than before
- cinematic combat as Bigby Wolf
- branching choices with lasting consequences

The listing also mentions investigating crimes, interrogating suspects and exploring a "fractured" Fabletown. Your choices are said to decide whether Bigby's legacy becomes one of redemption or ruin. These are the publisher's descriptions of its intended design. We haven't played the game and can't say how much your choices change the story.

## What's still unconfirmed

- **Release date or window:** not announced.
- **Console versions:** Telltale's page says the game is coming to more platforms, but we couldn't confirm which ones.
- **Episodic or complete release:** the first game came out in episodes. The current listing doesn't say whether the sequel will.
- **System requirements:** Steam asks only for a 64-bit version of Windows and gives no hardware details.
- **Price:** no price is listed.

## Avoiding old information

The sequel was first announced years ago, and early articles quoted plans that are now out of date. If you see a release window in an older article, check it against the current Steam listing before trusting it. If you want to avoid story spoilers, the store page and Telltale's short news posts carry release news without plot details.

